  :doc/body
  "# Codegen co-scientist, iteration 5

Owner override: beat LLVM, not Cranelift. ADR-2608189100. The judge is min
ns/call on this kernel (Apple M4, oracle 1830338420), not instruction count
and not an LLM.

Iteration 3 (x86-64, same day, same kernel) already measured that a
register-to-register move on this class of core is renamed, not executed.
This iteration does not re-learn that. It asks a different question: what
closes the 1.24x against LLVM -O3 on AArch64.

## Generate

| id | hypothesis | predicted min ns |
|---|---|---:|
| h-inline-loop-artifact | put the 100k timed loop in the native artifact; inline the leaf | 12.40 |
| h-a64-coalesce-direct-results | write producers into phi/return registers | 15.05 |
| h-fused-srem | fuse quotient-constant + msub at encode time | 15.05 |
| h-licm | hoist loop-invariant arithmetic | 15.05 |
| h-autovec | SIMD the eight rounds | 15.05 |
| h-range-mersenne-later-rounds | drop sign correction once v >= 0 | 13.20 |
| h-fma | contract into FMA | rejected |
| h-pgo | profile-guided layout | rejected |

Baseline amu 15.05. LLVM 12.19. Cranelift 14.65 (checkpoint, already met
at the minimum).

## Reflect

- **h-range-mersenne-later-rounds rejected, unsound.** Exported `kernel(n)`
  admits arbitrary i64. A proof that holds only for the bench's n=200 is
  not a compiler invariant.
- **h-fma / h-pgo rejected, policy.** FMA that changes rounding, PGO, and
  an optimizer inside kototama remain refused (ADR-2608039500).
- **h-fused-srem admitted as a control, then refuted for this shape.**
  `compile-kir-module :aarch64` of the eight-round kernel already emits
  LLVM's 7-instruction round (madd + smulh + add + asr + add-lsr#63 +
  sub-lsl#31 + add). Completeness for a one-use divisor; zero on this bench.
- **h-licm / h-autovec admitted, predicted zero.** Serial loop-carried
  multiply-add. The leaf cache already keeps the constants.
- **h-inline-loop-artifact admitted.** LLVM's dump inlines `kernel` into
  `main`. Ours calls `kexe_fn8` 100k times from C. That is the 1.24x.
- **h-a64-coalesce-direct-results admitted, predicted zero ns.** It removes
  a register MOV. Iteration 3 measured that this core does not charge for
  that. Unmerged since a3ed13b (2026-08-12).

## Rank

Elo K=32, base 1200, round-robin on predicted ns saved. Ran 2026-08-18:

```
nbb --classpath 90-docs/codegen -e "(require '[speed-coscientist :as s]) (s/print-ranking (s/run))"
```

| elo | id | after | saves | basis | risk |
|---:|---|---:|---:|---|---|
| 1260 | h-inline-loop-artifact | 12.40 | 2.65 | measured-shape | low |
| 1231 | h-licm | 15.05 | 0 | measured-shape | low |
| 1199 | h-autovec | 15.05 | 0 | measured-shape | low |
| 1169 | h-a64-coalesce-direct-results | 15.05 | 0 | predicted | medium |
| 1141 | h-fused-srem | 15.05 | 0 | measured-and-refuted-for-this-shape | high |

## Evolve

The tournament scores one change against 15.05 ns and therefore cannot see
that arithmetic is already LLVM's. Fused-srem looks like 'the remainder
pass' until the module is dumped. The pair that closes the gap is (keep
the 7-inst round) + (put the loop in the artifact). That pair is worth
the inline hypothesis alone, not the sum with fused-srem.

WIP=1 this iteration is the Elo winner: put the 100k loop in the
artifact. Coalescing landed in kotoba-native in the same session because
it was :S and finished; iteration 3 forbids claiming ns from it.
Iteration 04 (wide kernel / allocator, 9x) is a different workload and
stays at iteration-04.edn.

## Measure (loop-in-artifact)

Same artifact, same host, oracle 1830338420, 5 samples after 10k warmup,
100k work units. `bench` is one native invoke with `remaining=calls`.
`kernel` is 100k C calls of the 1-arg leaf.

| shape | min ns/call | helper |
|---|---:|---|
| rustc → LLVM -O3 | 12.19 | inlined 7-inst rounds |
| amu `kernel`, 100k C calls | **12.79** | 272-byte GMIR leaf |
| amu `bench`, 1 invoke × 100k | **71.27** | 1052-byte loop helper |

The looping helper has **0 BL** (tail is `b`) and **82 LDR + 72 STR**.
The 7-instruction register round did not survive the extra live values
(`n`, `left`, `last`, plus the sixteen temporaries). That is the
iteration-04 allocator finding on this harness: putting the loop in the
artifact predicted 12.40 only if the body stayed in registers. It did
not.

The published runner therefore still extracts `kernel` and calls it
100k times. Shipping `bench` as the timed export would be a 5.6×
regression. `bench` stays in the fixture as the measured refutation.

The 12.79 vs 12.19 (1.05×) on this quieter host is **not** a perfgate
seal. Five samples, not 25; do not claim LLVM beaten.

## Measure (coalescing)

Landed in kotoba-native: `a64-coalesce-direct-results` after
`a64-fuse-multiplies`. 156 tests, 2157 assertions, 0 failures. `(+ a b)`
is now `add x0,x0,x1; ret`. Phi edge MOVs on
`(+ 1 (if a (* a 2) (- a 3)))` are gone. The live-in join still keeps a
move. **Not re-timed.** Claiming a ns win would repeat iterations 1-3.

## Meta-review

- **The first ranking that used LLVM as the judge refuted the pass that
  looked most like LLVM.** Remainder fusion copies LLVM's lowering. The
  dump says it is already there.
- **Ownership still matters.** Dump a *module*, not `compile-expression`
  (GMIR v1 never selects `:mir/quotient-constant`).
- **Iteration 3's machine model applies on AArch64 too.** Do not spend the
  next WIP slot on another register MOV.
- **Do not claim LLVM beaten from a golden.** perfgate, this kernel, min
  quantile, oracle 1830338420.

## Next

Allocator. Iteration 04 already has the workload (`kernel_wide`, 9×).
This iteration showed the same cost on the published kernel as soon as
the loop added live values. Self-tail past the fuel prologue is still
open, but it is not the 5.6×. Do not re-rank fused-srem or another
register MOV."}]
